gotta go fast we're glad that sonic got  the redesign he deserves when the  trailer for Sonic came out everyone was  already scratching their heads gone was  the character that we know and love from  the video game and in its place was a  creepy little blue boy with a full mouth  of photorealistic Cuban teeth it's safe  to say whoever was in charge of  character design definitely missed the  mark instead of serving us a fun-loving  Hedgehog who can run faster than any  cheetah they presented us with a little  demon from the inner circle of hell  today we'll be looking at how the  creators of the film changed  Sonic's look in an attempt to salvage  the film if you look at photos of the  original Sonic cartoon  he's extremely likable he's 50% Punk  with his blue mohawk and 50% cute with  his huge unblinking eyes Sonic first  came into the world as Sonic the  Hedgehog a Japanese video game series  created by Sega the franchise was  centered around the blue hedgehog  fighting his arch-nemesis dr. Eggman a  mad scientist with a moustache so big  it's almost a character in its own  Sonic's vibrant cobalt blue color was  chosen to match Sega's logo and his  shoes were inspired by Michael Jackson's  infamous boots it was said his  personality was based on Bill Clinton  and his can-do attitude we wonder what  Hilary has to say about this Sonic  quickly rivaled Nintendo's mascot Mario  and the video game became one of the  best-selling franchises of all time  grossing a hot little 5 billion dollars  by 2014 it's gone down in history as one  of the greatest games of all time and  has heavily influenced pop culture kids  dress up for him on Halloween and  self-respecting adults continue to get  his face tattooed on their bodies some  more tasteful than others he is a total  icon and yet somehow paramount managed  to mess it up in their first try at  bringing him to the big screen as we  said before when the trailer dropped in  2019 the internet set fire with fans  going off about how truly horrified they  were with the hyper-realistic sonic in  the original design he really looked  like a prepubescent boy trapped in a  mascot suit doomed never to escape it  got so much backlash that paramount was  forced to push back the movie's release  date in a 10  to fix their horrible mistake the team  brought an animator Tyson Hess to leave  the redesign and try to make sonic look  less like a Teenage Mutant Animorph and  more like his origin thankfully they  started by changing the eyes which were  a main part of the problem in the video  game Sonics eyes were joined but for  some reason the animators decided to  separate them which made him look more  human but not in a good way in the you  would want to avoid eye contact at all  times kind of way in the redesign  however they upgraded his entire face  his eyes got bigger and more cartoony  his nose became less like a dog snout  and more like a button and his human  teeth were thankfully swapped for some  normal cartoony looking chompers though  his eyes are still separated because of  their new size they no longer look  anatomically similar to an actual  Hedgehog which really is a godsend on  top of that his eyebrows also got more  defined which allowed him to have a  greater range of expression in the first  pass Sonic had knees elbows and calves  making him have a more defined bone  structure the animation team thankfully  decided to scrap this and upgraded his  body to be more loose and compact and  less rigid and creepy in round two with  the blue they made his torso more  defined and gave him a triangular shape  with broad shoulders and a dainty narrow  waist he also appeared to have visited  the salon and got a total hair makeover  his fur became more vibrant blue and  overall a lot smoother they also seem to  get rid of the weird Tufte fur patches  that we saw in the first trailer and  made his spikes more defined to resemble  the Sega version in addition they also  decided to give Sonic back his big white  gloves instead of just making his paws  fur white he also got bigger socks and a  better pair of red kicks in the second  trailer with the upgraded design Sonic  describes himself as a little blue ball  of super energy in an extremely handsome  package we think this is a cheeky little  nod to the animation team giving  themselves a pat on the back for playing  dr. Frankenstein and going back to the  workshop to spruce up their terrifying  monster so they managed to save the  character design but did they save the  movie itself now that it's out the  reviews are in and people are giving  their two cents overall the movie has a  pretty generic plot and is overly  predictable the plot goes like this in  order to escape the villains of his  planet  sonic voiced by Ben Schwartz uses his  magical portal  and lands on planet Earth after trying  to blow off some steam by running around  a field sonic accidentally emits an  electromagnetic pulse that shuts down  the power across the Pacific Northwest  the United States Department of Defense  then enlists dr. Robotnik played by Jim  Carrey to help find the source of the  outage and it is then that he tracks  down Sonic by then sonic has befriended  the good-hearted sheriff named Tom  played by James Marsden and is shacking  up with him Robotnik invades the house  but Tom and Sonic escape the rest of the  film we see them narrowly avoiding him  while trying to track down Sonic's bag  of rings that he needs to teleport they  are able to locate them at the  Transamerica Pyramid and from there he  teleports Tom and his wife Maddy to  safety while he takes on Robotnik and  his robots after a number of harrowing  fight sequences Robotnik is taken down  and sent to a planet made of mushrooms  while sonic moves in with Mady and Tom  as their strange blue alien roommate all  in all we were not impressed by the  flick but unfortunately the after  credits scene led us to believe that  there will be a sequel in it we'll see  tails an extraterrestrial  anthropomorphic fox emerging from a  portal searching for Sonic which  suggests that the story is not over and  we wish it was if we were to assign a  grade for the sonic movie it would be a  d-plus ultimately it was full of cliches  and embarrassing attempts at being  relatable for younger audiences  lest we forget sonic did the floss dance  not once but twice which was  cringe-worthy at best on top of that  there were jokes thrown around about  Olive Garden's unlimited pasta and many  references to Vin Diesel and the fast  and furious all of which fell flat  another thing that we realized is that  there was little to no reference to the  video game world that he comes from and  we were curious as to why this was one  reason we think is that for many  children watching the film this will be  their first introduction to Sonic the  character while we get that  nine-year-olds these days probably  aren't logging all their hours playing  Sonic and Mario Kart anymore we wish  they had incorporated more elements from  its origin we think that if we had seen  Sonic not in the human world but in his  own home it may have been more  interesting while the new and improved  design did help a little in our opinion  it didn't save the film although if they  had kept the original design it would  have been a total train wreck imagine if  this media  her film would started the original  sonic completely with his lanky body and  beady little eyes it would have gone  from kind of meth - totally roasted in  his new and improved body his sassy  character works he comes off as a kind  of irreverent troublemaker with a  penchant for speed we can't even imagine  what all his fast moving sequences would  have looked like with the old design  probably terrifying it would have been  just like watching the kid from Jumanji  when he's transforming into a monkey  moving at the speed of light and dodging  bullets incredibly awkward and confusing  there is something called the uncanny  valley which the original design falls  into it's a concept that suggests that  humans like to see robots looking  human-like but only up until a certain  point at some point their humanist  becomes eerie and unsettling it's like  they're recognizable but something is a  little off usually their features are  hyper real much like Sonic's teeth in  the original design his mouth is  picture-perfect it's as if he is  constantly flossing and is some kind of  expert in oral hygiene but apart from  dentists most sets of teeth aren't that  perfect which makes us question why  Sonic's would be sure you can chalk it  up to him being an alien and maybe he  has better healthcare or something but  when it comes down to it it's just  somehow scary in the first design he  looks over animated and to humid it kind  of reminds us of that scene in stranger  things when wills mom finds his  so-called body in the lake we know it's  probably not real and that fact alone is  probably the scariest part of the show  to see something you think you know well  but it's ever so slightly altered and  heightened though over the years  computer graphics have gotten so much  better and technology has allowed for  characters to become more realistic it  appears that the engineers have still  not figured out how to not freak us out  with their creations though Sonic has to  go back to the drawing board with its  original design and came back a whole  lot cuter it still isn't our top pick  for flick we would however like to give  Jim Carrey props for his portrayal of  Robotnik though the movie was somewhat  tedious Carrie's performance peppered in  some excitement as he returned to his  roots and gave us some Ace Ventura vibes  his use of physical comedy reminds us of  him at 30 playing characters like the  mask though it was fun to see him flex  we weren't overly impressed by james  marsden character he was your average  middle-aged white man  trying to do the right thing in a small  town we don't know about you but we're  tired of this character and it feels as  though we've seen it about 1 trillion  times in our opinion when the team  decided to change Sonic's CGI they  should have changed the plot and the  characters as well we would have liked  to see some original content and not  just a whole movie recycling other films  and cobbling together a weak collage  paramount if you're listening don't just  rely on a name that everyone knows to  carry a film next time we'd like to see  developed characters brand new plots  that haven't been done before and CGI  that doesn't give us nightmares please  and thank you our final thought though  Sonic is supposed to be a little  speedster we think this movie is going  nowhere fast what do you think of the  new Sonic was the CG I've redesigned  enough to make a quality movie centered  on lightning-quick  alien hedgehog let us know in the  comments and subscribe to the things for  more  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

